# web/vendor/ holds byte-exact copies of the extension's shipped UI, and
# check-ui-vendor.mjs authenticates those exact bytes against the committed
# hash manifest (which the Docker build runs too). Git must never normalize
# line endings here: the source files carry mixed EOLs, and a normalized blob
# checks out with different bytes than sync-ui hashed — which is invisible on
# the machine that ran sync-ui and breaks every fresh clone (Railway).
web/vendor/** -text
